WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.459 --> 00:00:07.599
How does one discover life on other planets?

00:00:07.599 --> 00:00:11.740
Well, the first thing you need are other planets.

00:00:11.740 --> 00:00:19.060
Going around our sun are 8 planets, plus Pluto
and a bunch of moons and lots of other stuff.

00:00:19.060 --> 00:00:25.099
But it’s a small selection, so your best
bet is to look for planets going around any

00:00:25.099 --> 00:00:26.960
and all stars.

00:00:26.960 --> 00:00:32.210
Our galaxy alone has 100 billion stars in
it, and so there’s a lot of hope of seeing

00:00:32.210 --> 00:00:37.040
an enormous amount of planets as long as we
have a way of seeing them.

00:00:37.040 --> 00:00:40.859
Here are some ways you can see planets going
around other stars.

00:00:40.859 --> 00:00:43.109
The first is the transit method.

00:00:43.109 --> 00:00:50.170
The transit method is a method of seeing a
planet by watching for it block the light

00:00:50.170 --> 00:00:51.600
of the star.

00:00:51.600 --> 00:00:56.670
In other words, if the planet is reasonably
big compared to the star, when it orbits the

00:00:56.670 --> 00:01:02.980
star it could get in our way and we would
see that the light from the star dims and

00:01:02.980 --> 00:01:08.280
then brightens again with a very specific
pattern which would be caused by a planet

00:01:08.280 --> 00:01:10.180
transiting in front of it.

00:01:10.180 --> 00:01:15.540
And in fact at this point thousands of planets
going around other stars have been seen using

00:01:15.540 --> 00:01:16.619
the transit method.

00:01:16.619 --> 00:01:23.979
A second method that people use is a method
basically looking for the wobble of a star.

00:01:23.979 --> 00:01:30.130
A planet like Jupiter can be quite heavy even
compared to the star such that when it goes

00:01:30.130 --> 00:01:36.450
around the star, the star wobbles, and when
it wobbles towards and away from us it shifts

00:01:36.450 --> 00:01:41.039
the frequency of light that’s coming toward
us, it’s called the Doppler shift.

00:01:41.039 --> 00:01:47.380
And that Doppler shift happening at a very
regular pattern, period tells us that there’s

00:01:47.380 --> 00:01:49.030
something heavy going around it.

00:01:49.030 --> 00:01:56.140
A third way is if stars and planets pass in
between us and more distant bright stars.

00:01:56.140 --> 00:02:00.399
That passing can cause the light to be warped
a little bit.

00:02:00.399 --> 00:02:04.140
It’s called gravitational lensing, predicted
by Einstein.

00:02:04.140 --> 00:02:10.580
All these methods and more are hopes for seeing
thousands, tens of thousands, even hundreds

00:02:10.580 --> 00:02:16.690
of thousands of planets in the near and immediate
future.

00:02:16.690 --> 00:02:20.910
But then you want to figure out if there’s
life on any of those planets.

00:02:20.910 --> 00:02:22.830
How are we going to do that?

00:02:22.830 --> 00:02:26.250
Well the best bet is to look at the atmosphere.

00:02:26.250 --> 00:02:31.780
The atmosphere will contain all kinds of chemicals
and those chemicals could have been naturally

00:02:31.780 --> 00:02:37.440
there due to the formation of the planet in
the first place or they could be there because

00:02:37.440 --> 00:02:41.440
something interesting is happening on the
surface of the planet.

00:02:41.440 --> 00:02:49.250
Giant planets like Jupiter and bigger naturally
have water in their atmospheres but tiny rocky

00:02:49.250 --> 00:02:55.850
planets shouldn’t and they shouldn’t because
sunlight breaks apart water and hydrogen is

00:02:55.850 --> 00:02:59.810
so light it wants to escape light planets.

00:02:59.810 --> 00:03:05.420
So look for small rocky planets that have
lots of water in their atmosphere.

00:03:05.420 --> 00:03:11.400
Already that will suggest that there’s water
on the surface of the rocky planet, like oceans.

00:03:11.400 --> 00:03:16.840
It doesn’t prove there’s life on the planet
but at least now we’re getting more evidence

00:03:16.840 --> 00:03:21.010
and we’re seeing ways of seeing planets
that look more and more like the Earth.

00:03:21.010 --> 00:03:26.210
A final stage would be to look at that atmosphere
and find other things in the atmosphere with

00:03:26.210 --> 00:03:31.670
abundances, amounts that are unexpected to
occur simply naturally.

00:03:31.670 --> 00:03:34.340
One of those for example is oxygen.

00:03:34.340 --> 00:03:38.300
Oxygen can be something which is produced
by living organisms.

00:03:38.300 --> 00:03:46.140
So if you look at a planet and in its atmosphere
there’s water and there’s large levels

00:03:46.140 --> 00:03:51.440
of oxygen and perhaps other chemicals that
we might expect to be produced by the processes

00:03:51.440 --> 00:03:56.560
of life, then we start to have strong evidence
for the existence of life.

00:03:56.560 --> 00:04:02.420
To really go the final step you need really
provable theoretical models of what life can

00:04:02.420 --> 00:04:08.740
and cannot do and what nonlife processes can
do to put chemicals into the atmosphere too.

00:04:08.740 --> 00:04:11.600
How are we going to be sure?

00:04:11.600 --> 00:04:12.690
We don’t know.

00:04:12.690 --> 00:04:17.290
Other than let’s say direct communication
with the intelligent beings out there.

00:04:17.290 --> 00:04:23.240
However, we do see a path to get closer and
closer to eventually answering that question:

00:04:23.240 --> 00:04:23.849
Are we alone?

